s two records, false since r5 deleted the probe record). Two instances is a class, so the fix is structural:\n\n- **Rule S1** (`crossPlatformSharingContract`) — one structured rule per sentence. **R32** derives each grant set from the target rows, cross-checks it against the record's own `consumedByTargets`, then requires the grant clause verbatim, the names inside it to equal the derived set, and *every other target named anywhere in the sentence* to be a declared non-grantee mention with its own clause.\n- **R33** — the same clauses must appear in the rationale `.md` (whitespace-normalised), so the two artifacts can't drift.\n- A count scan requires any \"N App Group record(s)\" claim to sit at a registered path and match the record list.\n\n**The count scan failed on its first run** on `appGroupLeastPrivilegeRule.ceremonyCostIsZero` — \"the **two** App Group records\" — a third stale claim neither the reviewer nor r5 spotted. Fixed.\n\nOne deliberate divergence, stated in the JSON as `whyTheMacOSHostIsNotNamed`: the corrected sentence excludes macOS **universally** rather than naming the macOS host as excluded. Naming a target is what went stale in the first place. Their textual gate passes.\n\n## F2 — the portal task's contract\n\n`TASK-260715-3jloqy`'s description, scope, AC and checklist corrected on the board to `c1AuthorizationScope` exactly. The removed AC2 clause (\"only on provider identifiers\") contradicted **r1**, not just r5 — R7 has required the NE entitlement on all eight rows since r2, so provider-only verification would have passed a portal state where neither macOS host App ID carries the capability, failing at first build *after* the ceremony. Pinned as **rule P1** and gated by a new script that reproduces their hand check: 14 failures / 20 checks before, exit 0 after.\n\n## Gates\n\n| gate | result |\n|---|---|\n| reviewer F1 `jq` gate | r5 `false`/exit 1 → r6 `true`/exit **0** |\n| self-check R1–R33 | 975 checks, exit **0** (r5: 846) |\n| negative gates | 117/117, exit **0** (r5: 92) — 2 mutate the `.md`, not the JSON |\n| r5→r6 preservation | 53/53, exit **0** |\n| board gate (P1) | exit **0** |\n| legacy / board validate / `swift test` | exit **0** / exit **0** / 335 tests, exit **0** |\n\nAll harnesses re-verified in place from the board resource layout. Two blank exit codes in the first transcript pass came from bash-only `PIPESTATUS` under zsh — both re-run without a pipeline, both 0, recorded in the log rather than smoothed over. No product source, spec, or generated project touched; no board element created, deleted, or re-parented.","ttft_ms":2017,"ttft_stream_ms":1503,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":1581862,"uuid":"9f462a8d-6772-4200-a3d5-d092d904a9a8"}
